    "turn_text": "Well, we're trying to solve the problems that the Biden administration has created. We've got high gas prices that I've ever experienced. We've got high inflation in my lifetime. We see a war in Ukraine. Russia has invaded us committing war crimes. And we're powerless to stop what's happening. It's very frustrating. I got a front row seat to the incompetence of the Biden administration. I mean, you know, this president is not doing a terrible job. I mean, I hate to say it, but you know, you can't even read off the teleprompter anymore. So here we are 15 months in. When President Trump left office, we were energy independent. We were in that exporter of energy. And now we are begging Venezuela, we're begging Iran, Russia, for oil and gas. And, you know, as we see right now, Russia is a native Ukraine and the West is powerless to stop them because they're all reliant on Russian gas. And they're literally sending billions and billions of dollars to Russia while we're trying to do these economic sanctions. It's just all these policies are out of our out of whack. President Biden said one thing that really stuck with me. He said, our values have caught. Our values have caught. And really, those are his values. Those are the less values. And those costs are being seen by Americans all over this country at the gas pump and in the grocery store. And they're being seen in Ukraine where people are dying because we are weak abroad. So I got to front row seat to the circus and we're count down the days until November, but it's definitely a challenge.",
